# Discord's updater host — the one the desktop client blocks on at startup ("Checking updates...").
# Measured 2026-09-12: the updater sends a 175-byte TLS 1.2 ClientHello with no supported_versions and
# no ALPN, and the DPI kills it. Thirteen desync variants were tried against it — seqovl from 100 to
# 681, zero- and TLS-pattern fills, fake+fooling=ts, nodrop, hostfakesplit, multidisorder — and none
# opened it, while a control run with no desync at all hung too. The client's OWN traffic is a
# 1785-byte TLS 1.3 ClientHello and the strategy handles it fine, so only this host needs the tunnel.
updates.discord.com
